      "rev_n_8_525431_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_525431_1",
        "node_id": "n_8_525431",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Ensure that the logic correctly identifies whether Tokitsukaze already has a valid mentsu (either a koutsu or a shuntsu) in her hand without prematurely returning 0 when checking for a shuntsu. Specifically, the current implementation might incorrectly identify a non-existent shuntsu due to the way the loop iterates over potential sequences. Instead, refactor the `check_shuntsu` function to properly validate all possible sequences within the given tiles.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5647612924599078752",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_8_525431_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_0ffd64daf3",
        "created_at": 1794458169.123355
      },
      "rev_n_4_763c9f_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_763c9f_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_763c9f",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (revised): Instead of checking all possible combinations of two additional tiles, focus on forming a mentsu by adding one tile at a time. Specifically, check if adding one tile can complete a koutsu or a shuntsu. If not, check if adding another tile can complete either. This approach ensures that the minimum number of tiles required is found efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8182491802364944766",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_763c9f_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_a825287329",
        "created_at": 1794458222.6134994
      },
      "rev_n_10_302c40_0": {
